1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,825
Italy's population peaked in 2014, at 60.7 million.

2
00:00:06,225 --> 00:00:10,675
It has been falling ever since. Today, it's 59 million.

3
00:00:11,075 --> 00:00:15,275
On the United Nations' central projection, the fall speeds up.

4
00:00:16,075 --> 00:00:19,250
By 2050: about 52 million.

5
00:00:19,650 --> 00:00:24,675
By 2100: 35 million. Fewer than in 1950.

6
00:00:25,075 --> 00:00:30,706
Very few births, about 1.2 children per woman, and a median age of 48.

7
00:00:30,706 --> 00:00:33,200
The full story is in our video.
